  "content": {
    "id": "p83-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p83-q14-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A food stall normally sells 80 sandwiches per day for $6 each. For every 25-cent increase in price, daily sales fall by 2 sandwiches.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p83-q14-variable",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Let ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "x",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " be the number of 25-cent increases, where ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "x",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is a non-negative integer.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p83-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p83-q14-a-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Show that the revenue is",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p83-q14-a-given",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "R=\\left(6+\\frac{x}{4}\\right)(80-2x).",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Price $=6+\\frac{x}{4}$ dollars; sales $=80-2x$ sandwiches. Revenue $=\\text{price}\\times\\text{sales}=\\left(6+\\frac{x}{4}\\right)(80-2x)$.",
          "worked": "After $x$ increases, the price in dollars is $6+0.25x=6+\\frac{x}{4}$ and the number sold is $80-2x$ sandwiches. Revenue is price multiplied by the number sold, so\n$$R=\\left(6+\\frac{x}{4}\\right)(80-2x).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p83-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Express $R$ in general form.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=-\\frac12x^2+8x+480$.",
          "worked": "Expanding,\n$$\\begin{align*}R&=480-12x+20x-\\frac12x^2\\\\R&=-\\frac12x^2+8x+480.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p83-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Express $R$ in vertex form.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=-\\frac12(x-8)^2+512$.",
          "worked": "Complete the square:\n$$\\begin{align*}R&=-\\frac12(x^2-16x)+480\\\\R&=-\\frac12\\left((x-8)^2-64\\right)+480\\\\R&=-\\frac12(x-8)^2+512.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p83-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the price, number of sales and maximum daily revenue.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Price: $\\$8$; sales: 64 sandwiches; maximum daily revenue: $\\$512$.",
          "worked": "The coefficient of $(x-8)^2$ is negative, so the maximum occurs at $x=8$, an allowed non-negative integer.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Price}&=6+\\frac84\\\\\\text{Price}&=8\\text{ dollars}\\\\\\text{Sales}&=80-2(8)\\\\\\text{Sales}&=64\\text{ sandwiches}\\\\R_{\\max}&=512\\text{ dollars}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe stall should charge $\\$8$, sell 64 sandwiches and earn a maximum daily revenue of $\\$512$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
